The design for this work is in docs/nested-repos-design.md.

GitIgnore (gitIgnore.d): read .gitignore into a data structure in the constructor; write() writes it back.
Check .gitignore's managed block for syntax and sort order, and rewrite it if --fix is given.

GitRepos (gitRepos.d): read .gitrepos into a data structure in the constructor; write() writes it back.
Check .gitrepos for syntax and sort order.

ParentDirectory (parentDirectory.d): check agreement between .gitignore and .gitrepos, and with the disk, and rewrite one, the other, or both if --fix is given.

Then do the add-nested or pull-nested logic on top of ParentDirectory and write the files out.
